# Day 8 — Bugle. 6 September. Cool and breezy. The elk come down. A count, by ear, at dusk.
# Ruth called Basin.

call D8_AM
  day 8
  time 06:20-12:00
  kind report
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Morning. It's cold down here. Readings?
choice
  > "Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Wind {wind}." if obs_am set gave_readings -> read
  > "It's cold up here too." -> cold
node read
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Dry bulb {dry}, wet {wet}. Humidity {rh}. Wind {wind}. Fuel stick {fuel}.
DOT  Copy. First morning under fifty. Season's turning.
goto plan
node cold
THEO Basin, Kestrel. It's cold up here too.
DOT  That's not a reading, Kestrel, that's a complaint.
node plan
DOT  Fish and Game wants an elk count. By ear. At dusk, from the meadow. The bulls come down to bugle.
DOT  I told them you're a professional listener. Don't make me a liar.
do errand At dusk, sit on the log in Larkspur Meadow and count the bulls by ear.

call D8_DUSK
  day 8
  time 18:30-22:00
  where seat:2
  after D8_AM
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. You at the meadow?
THEO On the log. It's getting dark.
DOT  Good. Now be quiet and listen. Call me when you have a number. Basin out.
do elk

call D8_COUNT
  day 8
  needs elk_done
  kind initiated
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Elk count.
DOT  Go ahead.
choice
  > "Three." -> three
  > "Four." -> four
  > "Five." -> five
  > "I lost count." -> lost
node three
THEO Three bulls.
DOT  Three. Augie always said three. I'll put four, he always undercounted the one by the creek.
goto out
node four
THEO Four. One of them's down by the creek. He's the loudest.
DOT  Four. Augie always said three. Huh. Four it is.
goto out
node five
THEO Five. Maybe five.
DOT  Five, maybe. Fish and Game loves a maybe. I'll put four.
goto out
node lost
THEO I lost count. I was listening to them instead.
DOT  ...That's allowed. I'll put four. There's always four.
node out
do errand_done
DOT  Thank you, Kestrel. Basin out.

call D8_RUTH
  day 8
  time 20:00-26:00
  after D8_AM
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. My sister called. Here. On the land line. Nobody calls the land line.
THEO Is she alright?
DOT  She's fine. She's always fine. She wants me at Christmas. She wants me at Christmas every year.
DOT  Anyway. How's the wind up there?
choice
  > "Tell me about Ruth." set ruth_asked -> ask
  > "Wind's light. Northwest." -> letgo
  > [say nothing] -> quiet
node ask
THEO Tell me about Ruth.
DOT  ...She's older. She's in Calder. She has our mother's piano and nobody's played it since 2009.
DOT  She'd like you. Everybody likes people who listen.
DOT  How's the wind up there, Kestrel?
THEO Light. Northwest.
DOT  Copy. Goodnight.
end
node letgo
THEO Wind's light. Northwest.
DOT  Copy. ...Thank you. Goodnight, Kestrel.
end
node quiet
DOT  ...Goodnight, Kestrel.

call D8_EVE
  day 8
  time 16:30-18:20
  retry 19:00
  kind report
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Evening readings before you head down.
choice
  > "Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Wind {wind}." if obs_pm set gave_readings -> read
  > "Heading down now." -> down
node read
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Humidity {rh}. Wind {wind}.
DOT  Copy. Take a jacket. Basin out.
end
node down
THEO Heading down now.
DOT  Take a jacket. Basin out.
